-- Q3505: Data Management and Lifecycle [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Creating new data records from original source transactions in the system","Permanently destroying data that has exceeded its required retention period","Moving inactive data to lower-cost storage while retaining it for compliance","Processing raw transactional data into meaningful information for reporting"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Data archival involves moving inactive data to cost-effective long-term storage while retaining it for legal or regulatory requirements, per COBIT 2019 DSS06.06 and NIST SP 800-88. Archived data is typically read-only and infrequently accessed.
Wrong (A): Creating new data from source transactions describes data creation or generation, which is an earlier phase of the data lifecycle, not archival.
Wrong (B): Permanently destroying data describes data destruction or disposal, which occurs only after the retention period expires. Archival preserves data.
Wrong (D): Processing raw data into meaningful information describes data transformation or analysis, not the archival process of relocating inactive records.$EXPL$
