Wrong (C): ETL extracts copies of source data. Source systems retain their original data regardless of whether the ETL transform step succeeds or fails.
Wrong (D): A silent failure by definition produces no error message. Users see reports that appear normal, making the inaccuracy harder to detect.$EXPL$
