UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Ignore the discrepancy since it falls below the established materiality threshold","Run a reconciliation query to identify specific records causing the difference","Assume the general ledger is correct and adjust the subledger to match it","Delete the entire subledger and recreate it using general ledger balances"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per AICPA Trust Services Criteria PI1.4, data discrepancies require systematic investigation. The auditor should first perform a detailed reconciliation to isolate specific records causing the $47,000 difference, revealing whether the issue stems from unposted batches, entry errors, or unauthorized adjustments.
Wrong (A): Ignoring a discrepancy without investigation violates auditing standards. The $47,000 difference may indicate fraud or systemic errors regardless of materiality.
Wrong (C): Assuming either system is correct without investigation could mask the root cause and propagate errors through financial statements.
Wrong (D): Deleting and recreating the subledger destroys audit evidence and does not identify the root cause of the discrepancy.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3531;
